IMPORT prelude

-- Hijacking of Aircraft and Protection of Aircraft and International Airports Act 1978 (Singapore) -- when an aircraft is "in
-- flight" and "in service" (s 2(2)), the reach of the Act over military, customs and police aircraft (ss 3(2), 5(5), 5A(3), 5B(3),
-- 5C(3), 5D(4), 6(6)), hijacking (s 3), violence connected with a hijacking (s 4), destroying or endangering an aircraft
-- (s 5), false information endangering an aircraft in flight (s 6(3), (4)), violence and disruption at international airports
-- (s 7(1), (2)(a)(i), (b)), credible threats (s 8(1)), penalties (s 9), the liability of company officers (s 9A(2), (5)), the Public Prosecutor's
-- consent (s 10) and extradition (s 11(1), (5), (6)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (the deposit's page footer reads "version in force from 1/7/2025"), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HAPAIAA1978.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 3 of 2021 (Guns, Explosives
-- and Weapons Control Act 2021) wef 1 July 2025, to the definition of "act of violence" in s 2(1); most of the text carries
-- annotations to Act 10 of 2022 wef 1 September 2022. The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with
-- the body (it numbers "Interpretation" as 3 and "Hijacking" as 4); this row follows the body's numbers.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. It is requirement REQ-0123 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. A passenger, airline or airport business meets it through hijacking, sabotage, false
-- information, airport violence and threats, and through the penalties and the officer liability that follow.
--
-- Not encoded: ss 5A to 5D (using an aircraft as a weapon, BCN weapons, nuclear material) beyond their place in s 8(1) and the
-- penalty table; s 7(2)(a)(ii) and (4) (aircraft not in service at an airport); s 6(1), (2) (damage to air navigation facilities); s 8(2) (assisting an offender to evade) beyond its penalty;
-- s 9A(1) and 9B (state of mind of corporations; unincorporated associations and partnerships); s 11(2) to (4) and s 12
-- (extradition without a treaty, mutual assistance); and the definitions of BCN weapon and nuclear material. Whether conduct is
-- "unlawful" or an "act of violence" depends on other written law (s 2(1)) and is taken as a given fact.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Hijacking of Aircraft and Protection of Aircraft and International Airports Act 1978 -- offences`

§§ `2(2) -- in flight and in service`

-- s 2(2)(a): "the period during which an aircraft is in flight is deemed to include any period from the moment when all its
-- external doors are closed following embarkation until the moment when any such door is opened for disembarkation, and, in the
-- case of a forced landing, any period until the competent authorities take over responsibility for the aircraft".
-- (b): an aircraft is "in service during the whole of the period which begins with the pre-flight preparation of the aircraft for
-- a flight and ends 24 hours after the aircraft lands having completed that flight", and also at any time it is in flight.
-- The 24th hour itself is taken to be inside the period (an inference: "ends 24 hours after" does not say).
DECLARE Flight HAS
    `pre-flight preparation has begun` IS A BOOLEAN
    `external doors closed after embarkation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a door opened for disembarkation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made a forced landing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the authorities have taken over` IS A BOOLEAN
    `landed having completed the flight` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours since landing` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the flight` IS A Flight
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aircraft is in flight` IF
        (`the flight`'s `external doors closed after embarkation` AND (NOT `the flight`'s `a door opened for disembarkation`))
    OR  (`the flight`'s `made a forced landing` AND (NOT `the flight`'s `the authorities have taken over`))

GIVEN `the flight` IS A Flight
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aircraft is in service` IF
        `the aircraft is in flight` `the flight`
    OR  (    `the flight`'s `pre-flight preparation has begun`
         AND (   (NOT `the flight`'s `landed having completed the flight`)
              OR `the flight`'s `hours since landing` AT MOST 24))

§§ `3(2), 5(5), 5A(3), 5B(3), 5C(3), 5D(4), 6(6) -- military, customs and police aircraft`

-- Each offence applies "whatever the nationality or citizenship of the person, whatever the State in which the aircraft is
-- registered" and in Singapore or elsewhere -- but NOT to an aircraft "used in military, customs or police service" unless
-- (a) the person is a citizen of Singapore [s 3(2)] / the act is committed outside Singapore by a citizen [ss 5(5) etc.];
-- (b) the act is "committed in or over Singapore" [s 7(4): "in Singapore"]; or (c) the aircraft is used in the military, customs
-- or police service of the Republic of Singapore. The two wordings of the citizen limb give the same result, because an act in or
-- over Singapore is caught by (b) anyway.
DECLARE AircraftUse IS ONE OF
    `civil`
    `foreign military, customs or police service`
    `Singapore military, customs or police service`

DECLARE Means IS ONE OF
    `the use of force`
    `threats`
    `technological means`
    `stealth or persuasion only`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `hijacking (s 3)`
    `destroying or endangering an aircraft (s 5)`
    `using an aircraft to cause death or serious damage (s 5A)`
    `releasing or using a BCN weapon (s 5B, 5C)`
    `transporting a BCN weapon (s 5D)`
    `damaging air navigation facilities (s 6(1))`
    `communicating false information (s 6(3))`
    `violence or disruption at an international airport (s 7)`
    `a credible threat (s 8(1))`
    `assisting an offender to evade justice (s 8(2))`
    `no offence`

DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `aircraft use` IS AN AircraftUse
    `in or over Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intentional` IS A BOOLEAN
    `aircraft in service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `aircraft in flight` IS A BOOLEAN
    `seizes or exercises control of the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `means of control` IS A Means
    `destroys the aircraft or damages it so as to disable or endanger it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `commits on board an act of violence likely to endanger the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `places a device or substance likely to destroy or endanger the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
    `communicates false or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information endangers or is likely to endanger an aircraft in flight` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believed it true on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `communicated it in good faith in lawful employment duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at an aerodrome serving international civil aviation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by means of a device, substance or weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an act of violence likely to cause death or serious personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `endangers or is likely to endanger the aerodrome or persons there` IS A BOOLEAN
    `destroys or seriously damages aerodrome facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disrupts the aerodrome's services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `threatens to commit` IS AN Offence
    `the threat is credible` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches the aircraft` IF
        `the conduct`'s `aircraft use` EQUALS `civil`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `aircraft use` EQUALS `Singapore military, customs or police service`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `in or over Singapore`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `by a Singapore citizen`

§§ `3 -- hijacking`

-- s 3(1): "a person who unlawfully and intentionally seizes or exercises control of an aircraft in service by the use of force or by
-- threats of any kind, or by any technological means, commits the offence of hijacking". Control taken by none of these means
-- (stealth or persuasion alone) is outside the words.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is hijacking` IF
        `the Act reaches the aircraft` `the conduct`
    AND `the conduct`'s `unlawful`
    AND `the conduct`'s `intentional`
    AND `the conduct`'s `aircraft in service`
    AND `the conduct`'s `seizes or exercises control of the aircraft`
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `means of control` EQUALS `stealth or persuasion only`)

§§ `4 -- violence connected with a hijacking`

-- s 4: "Any act of violence against the passengers or crew of an aircraft in service done by a person in connection with the offence
-- of hijacking committed or attempted by him or her on board that aircraft is deemed to have been committed in Singapore",
-- wherever it was committed. It is then punishable "under the law in force in Singapore applicable thereto", not under s 9.
GIVEN `against passengers or crew` IS A BOOLEAN, `the aircraft was in service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in connection with a hijacking the same person committed or attempted on board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the violence is deemed committed in Singapore` IF
        `against passengers or crew`
    AND `the aircraft was in service`
    AND `in connection with a hijacking the same person committed or attempted on board`

§§ `5 -- destroying, damaging or endangering an aircraft`

-- s 5(1): a person who unlawfully and intentionally "(a) destroys an aircraft in service or so damages the aircraft as to render it
-- incapable of flight or as to be likely to endanger its safety in flight; or (b) commits on board an aircraft IN FLIGHT any act of
-- violence which is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft". (2): "places or causes to be placed on an aircraft in service
-- any device or substance which is likely to destroy the aircraft" or so damage or endanger it.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 5(1)` IF
        `the Act reaches the aircraft` `the conduct`
    AND `the conduct`'s `unlawful`
    AND `the conduct`'s `intentional`
    AND (   (`the conduct`'s `aircraft in service` AND `the conduct`'s `destroys the aircraft or damages it so as to disable or endanger it`)
         OR (`the conduct`'s `aircraft in flight` AND `the conduct`'s `commits on board an act of violence likely to endanger the aircraft`))

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 5(2)` IF
        `the Act reaches the aircraft` `the conduct`
    AND `the conduct`'s `unlawful`
    AND `the conduct`'s `intentional`
    AND `the conduct`'s `aircraft in service`
    AND `the conduct`'s `places a device or substance likely to destroy or endanger the aircraft`

§§ `6(3), (4) -- false information`

-- s 6(3): "a person who intentionally communicates any information which is false, misleading or deceptive in a material particular,
-- where the communication of the information endangers the safety of an aircraft in flight or is likely to endanger" it. Unlike
-- ss 3, 5 and 7(2), the word "unlawfully" is absent. (4): "It is a defence for a person charged ... to prove that -- (a) he or she
-- believed, and had reasonable grounds for believing, that the information was true; or (b) ... he or she was lawfully employed to
-- perform duties which consisted of or included the communication of information and ... communicated the information in good
-- faith". The burden of the defence is on the accused.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 6(3)` IF
        `the Act reaches the aircraft` `the conduct`
    AND `the conduct`'s `intentional`
    AND `the conduct`'s `communicates false or misleading information`
    AND `the conduct`'s `the information endangers or is likely to endanger an aircraft in flight`
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `believed it true on reasonable grounds`)
    AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `communicated it in good faith in lawful employment duties`)

§§ `7 -- international airports`

-- s 7(1): "A person who by means of any device, substance or weapon intentionally commits at an aerodrome serving international
-- civil aviation any act of violence which -- (a) causes or is likely to cause death or serious personal injury; and (b) endangers
-- or is likely to endanger the safe operation of the aerodrome or the safety of persons at the aerodrome". No military carve-out.
-- (2): by means of any device, substance or weapon, unlawfully and intentionally "(a) destroys or seriously damages -- (i) property
-- used for the provision of any facilities at an aerodrome ...; or (ii) any aircraft which is at such an aerodrome but is not in
-- service; or (b) disrupts the services of such an aerodrome", in such a way as to endanger or be likely to endanger its safe
-- operation or the safety of persons there. (4) carves military, customs and police aircraft out of (2)(a)(ii) only.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 7(1)` IF
        `the conduct`'s `intentional`
    AND `the conduct`'s `at an aerodrome serving international civil aviation`
    AND `the conduct`'s `by means of a device, substance or weapon`
    AND `the conduct`'s `an act of violence likely to cause death or serious personal injury`
    AND `the conduct`'s `endangers or is likely to endanger the aerodrome or persons there`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 7(2)` IF
        `the conduct`'s `unlawful`
    AND `the conduct`'s `intentional`
    AND `the conduct`'s `at an aerodrome serving international civil aviation`
    AND `the conduct`'s `by means of a device, substance or weapon`
    AND `the conduct`'s `endangers or is likely to endanger the aerodrome or persons there`
    AND (   `the conduct`'s `destroys or seriously damages aerodrome facilities`
         OR `the conduct`'s `disrupts the aerodrome's services`)

§§ `8(1) -- credible threats`

-- s 8(1): a person who "(a) makes a threat to commit any offence under section 3, 5(1) or (2), 5A(1), 5B(1), 5C(1), 6(1) or 7(1) or
-- (2); or (b) unlawfully and intentionally causes any person to receive such a threat, under circumstances which indicate the threat
-- to be credible". The list leaves out s 5D(1) (transporting BCN weapons) and s 6(3) (false information), though s 8(2) lists both.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a threat to commit it is caught by section 8(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `hijacking (s 3)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `destroying or endangering an aircraft (s 5)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `using an aircraft to cause death or serious damage (s 5A)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `releasing or using a BCN weapon (s 5B, 5C)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `damaging air navigation facilities (s 6(1))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `violence or disruption at an international airport (s 7)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 8(1)` IF
        `a threat to commit it is caught by section 8(1)` (`the conduct`'s `threatens to commit`)
    AND `the conduct`'s `the threat is credible`

§§ `9 -- penalties`

-- s 9(1): a person guilty of an offence under this Act (other than under s 8(1) or (2)) is liable on conviction "(a) in the case of an
-- individual, to imprisonment for life; or (b) in any other case, to a fine not exceeding $1 million". No fine is provided for an
-- individual under (1). (2): s 8(1) -- an individual, "a fine not exceeding $500,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 10 years or ... both"; any other case, a fine not exceeding $1 million. (3): s 8(2) -- the same, but 7 years.
-- Whether "imprisonment for life" in (1)(a) is a fixed sentence or a maximum is not said in this Act; the row records only that the
-- individual is liable to it.
DECLARE Offender IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company or other non-individual`

GIVEN `the offender` IS AN Offender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offender is an individual` IF
    CONSIDER `the offender`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is under section 8` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a credible threat (s 8(1))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `assisting an offender to evade justice (s 8(2))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offender` IS AN Offender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offender is liable to imprisonment for life` IF
        `the offender is an individual` `the offender`
    AND (NOT `the offence is under section 8` `the offence`)
    AND (NOT `the offence` EQUALS `no offence`)

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offender` IS AN Offender
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `no offence` THEN 0
    ELSE IF NOT `the offender is an individual` `the offender` THEN 1000000
         ELSE IF `the offence is under section 8` `the offence` THEN 500000
              ELSE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offender` IS AN Offender
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum term of years` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offender is an individual` `the offender` THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `a credible threat (s 8(1))` THEN 10
         WHEN `assisting an offender to evade justice (s 8(2))` THEN 7
         OTHERWISE 0

§§ `9A(2), (5) -- officers of a corporation`

-- s 9A(2): where a corporation commits an offence under this Act, a person "(a) who is -- (i) an officer of the corporation; or
-- (ii) an individual involved in the management of the corporation and in a position to influence the conduct of the corporation in
-- relation to the commission of the offence; and (b) who -- (i) consented or connived, or conspired with others ...; (ii) is in any
-- other way ... knowingly concerned in, or is party to, the commission of the offence ...; or (iii) knew or ought reasonably to have
-- known that the offence ... would be or is being committed, and failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent or stop" it, "shall
-- be guilty of that same offence". (5): it "applies whether or not the corporation is convicted of the offence". (6): "corporation"
-- includes a limited liability partnership; "officer" includes a director, partner, chief executive, manager or secretary.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a director, partner, secretary or similar officer`
    `a manager in a position to influence the offending conduct`
    `a member of staff with no such position`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `consented, connived or conspired` IS A BOOLEAN, `knowingly concerned` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or ought to have known and failed to take reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN, `the corporation was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of the corporation's offence` IF
        (NOT `the role` EQUALS `a member of staff with no such position`)
    AND (   `consented, connived or conspired`
         OR `knowingly concerned`
         OR `knew or ought to have known and failed to take reasonable steps`)

§§ `10 -- the Public Prosecutor's consent`

-- s 10(1): "No prosecution shall be instituted under this Act without the written consent of the Public Prosecutor." (2): without it
-- "(a) a person may be arrested ...; (b) a warrant for the arrest ... may be issued and executed; (c) a person may be charged ...;
-- and (d) a person charged ... may be remanded in custody or granted bail, but no further steps in the proceedings ... are to be
-- taken until the consent of the Public Prosecutor has been obtained."
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `arrest`
    `issuing and executing an arrest warrant`
    `charging`
    `remand or bail`
    `trial`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step may be taken before the Public Prosecutor consents` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `trial` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `11(1), (5), (6) -- extradition`

-- s 11(1): "Every relevant offence is deemed to be an extradition offence under the Extradition Act 1968." (5): any relevant offence
-- "is deemed not to be an offence of a political character". (6): "relevant offence" means an offence under this Act, or an abetment
-- of or attempt to commit one, "(other than section 9A(2) or 9B(2))" -- so an officer's derivative liability is not extraditable
-- under this section.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `liable only as an officer under section 9A(2) or 9B(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an extradition offence and not political` IF
        (NOT `the offence` EQUALS `no offence`)
    AND (NOT `liable only as an officer under section 9A(2) or 9B(2)`)
